.TH DANBY-FORCEDPENDULUM 1
.SH NAME
danby-forcedpendulum \- periodically forced damped pendulum
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/forcedpendulum
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Forcedpendulum
integrates
.EX
theta'' + c theta' + sin(theta) = A cos(omega t).
.EE
It combines a directly manipulated physical pendulum, a phase portrait, an
angle time series, and a stroboscopic Poincare section.  Orange phase points
are sampled once per forcing period.  A periodic response produces a finite
set of points; a chaotic attractor produces a structured cloud.
.PP
The problem-specific equation and energy calculation reside in
.BR /dis/danby/forcedpendulum.dis ;
the application owns only integration, interaction, and presentation.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the pendulum to set its angle.  Bottom tracks control damping, driving
amplitude, and driving frequency.  Space pauses, period advances one numerical
step while paused,
.B R
resets, and Escape or
.B Q
exits.
.SH VALIDATION
The model regression test disables damping and forcing and checks conservation
of mechanical energy over twenty simulated seconds with RK4 step 0.001.
.SH SOURCE
.B /module/danby/forcedpendulum.m
.br
.B /appl/danby/plugin/forcedpendulum.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/forcedpendulum.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-chaos (1),
.IR numerics (2),
.IR plot (2)
